{"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostHogBatchEncoder"}],"externalID":"s:15PostHogEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"PostHogEncoding"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"PostHogBatchEncoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PostHogBatchEncoder"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder.swift#L83","fileName":"PostHogBatchEncoder.swift"}},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/init(projectToken:plan:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batch(of:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/encode(_:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatch"],"title":"Encoding batches","generated":true,"anchor":"Encoding-batches"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/posthogbatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of PostHog’s batch capture API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can send events to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/batch\/"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PostHogBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import Instrumentation","import PostHogEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan(schemas: [SignedUp.schema, SessionStarted.schema, SessionEnded.schema])","let postHog = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: batchURL,  \/\/ https:\/\/us.i.posthog.com\/batch\/, or your instance's","    instrument: NoOpInstrument(),  \/\/ no trace context in the request's header fields","    encoder: PostHogBatchEncoder(projectToken: projectToken, plan: plan))","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: postHog)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON object of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with two members: ","type":"text"},{"code":"api_key","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"project token, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one object per record, oldest first, with these members:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"text":", as it is","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s stored properties, by name, then the members listed below","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked: ISO 8601 in UTC, with milliseconds ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2026-11-23T14:03:27.512Z"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent, and every event is anonymous: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$process_person_profile: false"},{"type":"text","text":", so PostHog makes no person profile, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$geoip_disable: true"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so PostHog doesn’t add a location from the request’s IP address. A record with no session (one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracked by a tracker without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":", or one a store recovered after a relaunch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which keeps no context) is its own anonymous person, linked to nothing: PostHog rejects a whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch when one of its events has no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":". PostHog counts a person per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so its unique users are sessions. The session is also sent as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", which PostHog’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions and web analytics group events by ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":" is the UUIDv7 they require); a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no session has none. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context value, aren’t sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read from the event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" form, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" derives, through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types its schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a string; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a boolean; an integer, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Float","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a number; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" an ISO 8601 string, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uppercase UUID string; an array an array; and an optional’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is its value. A type the plan can’t map is written as its encoding holds it. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A property whose name starts with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which only a hand-written ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance can write, or is ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left out and logged at notice level, as PostHog reads those names as settings (","type":"text"},{"code":"$set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$process_person_profile","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or the identity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_namespace"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The bundle identifier, version and build, each left out when ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_model"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_type"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model, and "},{"code":"Mobile","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Tablet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Desktop","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"TV","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"Vision","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the form factor; no "},{"code":"$device_type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for a watch"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$locale","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"code":"en-US","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$network_wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$network_cellular","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi, and whether it is cellular"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name and version"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the body, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a name PostHog keeps for its own events), one whose event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or one that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds a value JSON can’t ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). Each is logged at error level;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batch(of:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSkippedRecord","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"s. When every record of a batch is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/encode(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" throws, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PostHog answers a batch it takes with 200, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" retries one that gets no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects. A record sent again keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The bytes are the same for the same records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes. PostHog takes a body of up to 20 MB, so keep"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batches far smaller ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"type":"text","text":" sends 20 records at most)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding"]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://PostHogEncoding/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding":{"abstract":[{"text":"Write batches of records for PostHog’s batch capture API, for an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to send.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding","kind":"symbol","title":"PostHogEncoding","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/PostHogSkippedRecord":{"abstract":[{"text":"A record ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" left out of a batch’s body, and wh